5 Filter for non-wear and out-of-range observations
Observations, i.e. simultaneous eye-level, chest-worn, and wrist-worn dosimeter measurements at the same point in time, were excluded if non-wear was indicated (i.e. sleep or non-wear reported by the participant in the logbook) or if any of the three measurements exceeded the operating range of the dosimeter (&gt; 100,000 lx melanopic EDI).

#| label: filter-nonwear-outofrange

remove_nonwear &lt;- function(data, site_name) {
  sleep &lt;- load_data("sleepdiaries", site = site_name)
  nonwear &lt;- load_data("wearlog", site = site_name)

  exclude_intervals &lt;- bind_rows(
    sleep |&gt; select(Id, int_start = sleepprep, int_end = out_ofbed),
    nonwear |&gt; select(Id, int_start = start, int_end = end)
  )

  data |&gt;
    ungroup() |&gt;
    anti_join(
      exclude_intervals,
      # Also removes observations with the exact "boundary" time stamp
      by = join_by(Id, Datetime &gt;= int_start, Datetime &lt;= int_end)
    ) |&gt;
    group_by(Id)
}

remove_high_medi &lt;- function(data) {
  data |&gt;
    filter(if_all(starts_with("MEDI_"), ~ . &lt; 1e5))
}

datasets &lt;- imap(datasets, remove_nonwear)
datasets &lt;- map(datasets, remove_high_medi)


# Count participants and participant-days
count_participants("Filtered for non-wear and out of range cases", datasets)

7 Import contextual data
Contextual data is added to each observation: time of day (hourly), day of experiment (integer counting from the first day) site name, photoperiod state (civil dawn and dusk, through LightLogR’s add_photoperiod() function (Zauner et al. 2025)), and light exposure diaries (the primary and secondary lightsource, and columns with booleans for the type of activity). The time of day is represented on an hourly basis using the midpoint of each hour (e.g. 08:00 to 09:00 is represented as 8.5).

#| label: import-contextual-data

# Add experiment day and time of day
# timeofday as hourly midpoint (e.g. 08:00-09:00 -&gt; 8.5)
add_day_time &lt;- function(data) {
  data |&gt;
    mutate(
      timeofday = hour(Datetime) + 0.5,
      day = factor(as.integer(as.Date(Datetime) - min(as.Date(Datetime))) + 1)
    )
}

# Add site name
add_site &lt;- function(data, name) {
  data |&gt;
    mutate(site = factor(name))
}

# Add photoperiod state
add_photoperiodstate &lt;- function(data, coords) {
  add_photoperiod(data, coords) |&gt;
    mutate(photoperiod.state = factor(photoperiod.state)) |&gt;
    select(-dawn, -dusk, -photoperiod)
}

# Add light exposure diaries
add_diary &lt;- function(data, site_name) {
  diary &lt;- load_data("lightexposurediary", site = site_name) |&gt;
    select(
      Id, start, end,
      lightsource_primary, lightsource_secondary,
      act_sleep, act_home, act_road_vehicle, act_road_open,
      act_working_indoor, act_working_outdoor, act_free_outdoor, act_other
    ) |&gt;
    mutate(end = end - seconds(1)) # e.g. 11:00:00 -&gt; 10:59:59 (to prevent 2 entries for one timestamp)

  data |&gt;
    ungroup() |&gt;
    left_join(
      diary,
      by = join_by(Id, Datetime &gt;= start, Datetime &lt;= end)
    ) |&gt;
    group_by(Id)
}

datasets &lt;- datasets |&gt;
  map(add_day_time) |&gt;
  # Imap also gives the index of the name of dataset
  imap(add_site) |&gt;
  # Coordinates loaded previously from general_parameters.R
  imap(\(data, name) add_photoperiodstate(data, coordinates[[name]])) |&gt;
  imap(add_diary)

9 Calculate placement errors
The placement errors (mean hourly log-transformed differences between eye-level and body-worn dosimeter measurements, in melanopic EDI) were computed using a paired-differences approach. As the eye-level and body-worn measurements were at (approximately) the same time stamp, they were conducted under the same illumination field. Computing the log-difference within each pair before averaging preserves this paired structure and allows investigation of the measurement error. The alternative of taking the log of each position’s hourly mean melanopic EDI discards the pairing and hence is thus only valid for an outcome focused analysis.
For placement position x, where x refers to either the chest- or wrist-worn dosimeter, the (hourly aggregated) placement error (relative to a dosimeter worn on a pair of glasses) is defined as
\[
\bar{D}_x = \frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left[\log_{10}(E_{x,i} + 0.1) - \log_{10}(E_{glasses,i} + 0.1)\right]
\]where \(E_{glasses,i}\) denotes the eye-level measurement and \(E_{x,i}\) denotes the measurement at position \(x\), both recorded at timestamp \(i\), and \(n\) is the number of measurements within the hour.

#| label: calculate-logdif-average

to_hourly &lt;- function(data) {
  data |&gt;
    ungroup() |&gt;
    mutate(
      absdif_c = MEDI_c - MEDI_h,
      absdif_w = MEDI_w - MEDI_h,
      logdif_c = log10(MEDI_c + 0.1) - log10(MEDI_h + 0.1),
      logdif_w = log10(MEDI_w + 0.1) - log10(MEDI_h + 0.1)
    ) |&gt;
    group_by(Id, timeofday, day, site, environment, act_context, work_light_context) |&gt;
    summarise(
      MEDI_h = mean(MEDI_h),
      MEDI_c = mean(MEDI_c),
      MEDI_w = mean(MEDI_w),
      absdif_c = mean(absdif_c),
      absdif_w = mean(absdif_w),
      logdif_c  = mean(logdif_c),
      logdif_w = mean(logdif_w),
      photoperiod.state = names(which.max(table(photoperiod.state))),
      .groups = "drop"
    ) |&gt;
    mutate(photoperiod.state = as.factor(photoperiod.state)) |&gt;
    arrange(Id, day, timeofday)
}

datasets &lt;- map(datasets, to_hourly)
